Subject: [PATCH] Update removed Qt APIs for Qt 6.11 compatibility

Keep the selected KeePassXC 2.7.12 core building against Qt 6.11 without
changing its KDBX semantics. The changes replace removed Qt APIs, add direct
includes that were previously transitive, keep optional KeeShare code out of
the headless core, and preserve KDBX4's 32-bit variant-map length fields now
that Qt container sizes use 64-bit qsizetype. It also makes PasswordGenerator's
ASCII code-point construction explicit after Qt 6.11 removed int-to-QChar
implicit conversion; the character sets and random algorithm are unchanged.

